  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Going to Bristol** (1 other source): Owen Pallett of Final Fantasy, the tour's openers, joined the band onstage playing violin on this song [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Handball**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **One Fine Day**: back after 23 archived shows (619 days); rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Song for Dana Plato**: rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Going to Michigan**: back after 118 archived shows (3331 days); rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Going to Bristol**: back after 117 archived shows (3143 days); rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Hebrews 11:40**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2009-11-28.aud.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 78 min [1]. Said about its sound: Peter's bass is mixed especially loud, and John's vocals are often buried in the mix [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Cotton, Deuteronomy 2:10, Enoch 18:14, No Children, Palmcorder Yajna, Psalms 40:2, Romans 10:9 [1]\n- Part of the band's first North American tour for The Life of the World to Come; Perry Owen Wright added electric guitar to the trio [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2009-11-28.aud.flac16**: taped by Thomas J Hartnett; transferred by Thomas J Hartnett; source: AUD>Zoom H2 recorder [1]",
